# KernelPatch / APatch compatibility.
# The miatoll defconfig enables Clang CFI (CONFIG_CFI_CLANG) and Shadow
# Call Stack (CONFIG_SHADOW_CALL_STACK). CFI injects a runtime check
# before every indirect call and panics on a type mismatch; KernelPatch
# redirects those calls to its own code, so the first hooked call trips
# CFI and the kernel panics at boot. SCS is incompatible for the same
# reason (it validates return addresses). Disable both on the
# APatch-pre-patched variants. ThinLTO stays on (CFI needs LTO, not
# the other way round); if APatch still fails to boot, disabling LTO
# is the next step.
# CONFIG_CFI_CLANG is not set
# CONFIG_CFI_CLANG_SHADOW is not set
# CONFIG_SHADOW_CALL_STACK is not set
